<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brunei People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1956">1956</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Parti Rakyat Brunei</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brunei People's Party was a political party founded in 1956 under the leadership of A. M. Azahari, calling for independence, democracy and the union of Brunei, Sarawak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> under the sultan. It won every elected seat in the 1962 elections to Brunei's Legislative Council, but in December 1962 its armed wing launched the Brunei revolt, which British forces quickly suppressed. The party was then banned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brunei-peoples-party.jpg" alt="Brunei People's Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NorthTension · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_PRB.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
